# Runtime and backend memory lowering

Physical memory strategies and the collector-free release guarantee.

## Contract

- Input: validated HIR; borrow facts; validated affine cleanup decisions; validated lifetime topology; `ValidatedMemoryPlan` containing allocation-family layouts, selected strategies, cleanup/destruction plans, REC decisions and physical coalescing decisions; selected function set; target assignment; import/export/capability plan; semantic layout identity; builder lifecycle/runtime plan
- Output: target-specific allocation, region, counted, garbage-collected and ownership representations
- Decides: realisation of the selected memory plan, handle-tag representation and conservative retention behaviour for already-legal topology
- Must not decide: source legality, borrow facts, region legality, memory-strategy selection, target partition or page lifecycle policy
- Invariant: every backend consumes the complete validated memory plan, preserves the same shared, exclusive, copy and move semantics, and a capable full-control release backend must not fall back to a tracing collector

## Planning order

[codeblock, $code("text"):
    validated HIR
        -> borrow and last-use analysis
        -> local allocation-family and retained-edge constraints
        -> exported lifetime and retention summaries
        -> project/package summary instantiation
        -> complete backend-neutral lifetime-topology validation
        -> non-lexical interval, frontier and epoch completion
        -> backend-neutral memory requirements
        -> target-affinity analysis and partition
        -> target-contract validation
        -> per-physical-variant family/layout refinement
        -> revalidate affected refined family-edge facts
        -> target/profile-aware compiler-owned memory planning
        -> ValidatedMemoryPlan
        -> backend lowering
        -> collector-free artefact verification where required
]

`check` runs through creation and validation of the `ValidatedMemoryPlan` and stops before backend lowering. Each `ValidatedMemoryPlan` is scoped to one target/profile physical variant. The compiler-owned memory planner chooses host GC versus affine, region, group or REC representation for that variant; lowerers only realise the selected plan. GC-native and collector-free variants share the same mandatory topology result.

